document "Minecraft Crafting"

description "A complete crafting guide for Minecraft Bedrock Edition."

section "Crafting Basics"

    text
        Crafting is one of the most important parts of Minecraft. It allows you to turn materials you collect into tools, weapons, blocks, armor, food, and many other useful items.

        Most crafting recipes are made by placing items into a crafting grid in a specific pattern.
    end

    subsection "The 2 × 2 Crafting Grid"

        text
            Your inventory contains a 2 × 2 crafting grid. This grid can be used to make simple recipes that require up to four crafting slots.

            You can open your inventory to access the 2 × 2 crafting grid.
        end

        list
            Open your inventory.
            Place the required materials into the crafting grid.
            Arrange the materials according to the recipe.
            Take the crafted item from the output slot.
        end

        note
            The 2 × 2 crafting grid cannot be used for recipes that require a 3 × 3 crafting grid.
        end

    end

    subsection "The Crafting Table"

        text
            A crafting table provides a 3 × 3 crafting grid. This allows you to craft many more items than the inventory crafting grid.
        end

        list
            Collect four wooden planks.
            Open your inventory.
            Place the four planks into the 2 × 2 crafting grid.
            Take the crafting table from the output slot.
            Place the crafting table in the world.
            Interact with the crafting table to open its 3 × 3 crafting grid.
        end

    end

end

section "Using The Crafting Table"

    subsection "Opening The Crafting Interface"

        text
            Place a crafting table in the world and interact with it. The crafting table interface contains a 3 × 3 crafting grid and an output slot.
        end

    end

    subsection "Placing Materials"

        text
            Place the required materials into the crafting grid. The position of each material matters for shaped recipes.

            Some recipes require a specific arrangement, while others only require the correct ingredients and do not care about their exact positions.
        end

    end

    subsection "Taking The Result"

        text
            When the materials match a valid recipe, the crafted item appears in the output slot.

            Select the output item to move the crafted item into your inventory.
        end

    end

end

section "Recipe Book"

    subsection "What Is The Recipe Book?"

        text
            The recipe book is an in-game crafting reference that shows recipes available to you.

            It can help you find recipes without having to memorize their crafting patterns.
        end

    end

    subsection "Using The Recipe Book"

        list
            Open your inventory or a crafting interface.
            Open the recipe book.
            Browse or search for a recipe.
            Select a recipe to view its requirements.
            Craft the item if you have the required materials.
        end

    end

    subsection "Recipe Availability"

        text
            Recipes may become available as you obtain or discover their required materials. The exact recipe-book behavior can depend on your game settings and version.
        end

        note
            A recipe appearing in the recipe book does not necessarily mean that you currently have enough materials to craft it.
        end

    end

end

section "Crafting Recipes"

    subsection "Shaped Recipes"

        text
            A shaped recipe requires materials to be arranged in a particular pattern.

            The positions of the ingredients in the crafting grid determine whether the recipe is valid.
        end

        code
            A B
            C D
        end

        text
            In a shaped recipe, changing the position of an ingredient can produce a different result or make the recipe invalid.
        end

    end

    subsection "Shapeless Recipes"

        text
            A shapeless recipe requires specific ingredients but does not require them to be placed in a particular pattern.

            The ingredients can generally be arranged in different positions within the crafting grid and still produce the same result.
        end

    end

    subsection "Recipe Output"

        text
            Recipes can produce one item or multiple items. The amount produced depends on the recipe.

            Some crafting operations also consume different amounts of materials depending on the recipe.
        end

    end

end

section "Crafting Materials"

    subsection "Wood"

        text
            Wood is one of the earliest and most useful crafting materials in Minecraft.

            Logs can be converted into planks, and planks can be used to create many basic items and blocks.
        end

        list
            Logs
            Stripped Logs
            Wood
            Stripped Wood
            Planks
            Sticks
        end

    end

    subsection "Stone"

        text
            Stone and related materials are used for stronger early-game tools, weapons, furnaces, building blocks, and other items.
        end

        list
            Cobblestone
            Stone
            Stone-related blocks
            Deepslate
        end

    end

    subsection "Ores And Metals"

        text
            Ores can provide materials that are used for tools, armor, blocks, and other crafted items.

            Some materials must be smelted or processed before they can be used in certain crafting recipes.
        end

        list
            Coal
            Iron
            Copper
            Gold
            Redstone
            Lapis Lazuli
            Diamond
            Emerald
        end

    end

    subsection "Other Materials"

        list
            Sticks
            String
            Leather
            Paper
            Sugar
            Glass
            Wool
            Flint
            Clay
            Nether materials
            End materials
        end

    end

end

section "Essential Early Game Crafting"

    subsection "Basic Items"

        list
            Crafting Table
            Sticks
            Torches
            Chest
            Furnace
            Bed
        end

    end

    subsection "Basic Tools"

        text
            Tools allow you to collect materials more efficiently and access resources that cannot easily be collected by hand.
        end

        list
            Pickaxe
            Axe
            Shovel
            Hoe
        end

    end

    subsection "Basic Weapons"

        list
            Sword
            Bow
            Crossbow
            Shield
        end

    end

    subsection "Basic Equipment"

        list
            Helmet
            Chestplate
            Leggings
            Boots
        end

    end

end

section "Crafting Progression"

    subsection "Early Game"

        text
            Early in a world, focus on crafting the equipment and utility blocks needed to gather resources and survive.

            Wooden tools can help you get started, while stone tools provide a significant improvement once you collect stone.
        end

    end

    subsection "Iron Equipment"

        text
            Iron allows you to create stronger tools, weapons, armor, buckets, shears, and many other useful items.
        end

    end

    subsection "Diamond Equipment"

        text
            Diamonds can be used to craft high-tier tools, weapons, and armor.

            Diamond equipment is highly durable and can later be upgraded through other systems.
        end

    end

    subsection "Netherite Equipment"

        text
            Netherite is used to upgrade diamond equipment. Netherite-related crafting requires materials obtained from the Nether.
        end

    end

end

section "Useful Crafting Blocks"

    subsection "Furnace"

        text
            A furnace is used primarily for smelting and cooking. It is different from a crafting table because it processes materials rather than using normal crafting recipes.
        end

    end

    subsection "Crafting Table"

        text
            The crafting table provides the 3 × 3 crafting grid required by many recipes.
        end

    end

    subsection "Chest"

        text
            Chests provide additional storage space for items and blocks.
        end

    end

    subsection "Other Utility Blocks"

        list
            Anvil
            Smithing Table
            Stonecutter
            Cartography Table
            Loom
            Grindstone
            Blast Furnace
            Smoker
            Brewing Stand
            Enchanting Table
        end

        note
            Some utility blocks have their own interfaces and systems rather than using normal crafting alone.
        end

    end

end

section "Crafting Tips"

    tip
        Keep extra wood available. Wooden planks and sticks are used in many early-game recipes.
    end

    tip
        Craft a crafting table early so you can access the full 3 × 3 crafting grid.
    end

    tip
        Use the recipe book when you do not remember a crafting pattern.
    end

    tip
        Store extra crafting materials in an organized storage system so important resources are easy to find.
    end

    tip
        Before crafting a large number of items, check how many materials the recipe consumes and how many items it produces.
    end

    tip
        Remember that some items are created through processes such as smelting, stonecutting, brewing, or smithing rather than ordinary crafting.
    end

end

section "Crafting And Inventory Management"

    subsection "Managing Materials"

        text
            Keep commonly used materials organized in your inventory or storage system.

            Materials such as wood, stone, iron, coal, and other frequently used resources are useful to keep available.
        end

    end

    subsection "Crafting In Large Quantities"

        text
            If you need many copies of an item, craft them in batches when possible. This can save time when preparing materials for a large build or project.
        end

    end

    subsection "Avoiding Waste"

        text
            Check the recipe before crafting expensive items. Some materials can be difficult to replace, especially during early progression.
        end

    end

end

section "Crafting Troubleshooting"

    subsection "The Recipe Does Not Work"

        list
            Check that you are using the correct materials.
            Check that the materials are placed in the correct positions.
            Check whether the recipe requires a 2 × 2 or 3 × 3 crafting grid.
            Check whether you are using the correct crafting interface.
            Check whether the recipe requires another crafting or processing station.
        end

    end

    subsection "The Recipe Is Not In The Recipe Book"

        text
            Check that you have obtained or discovered the materials required for the recipe.

            Recipe-book availability can also depend on game settings and the current Minecraft version.
        end

    end

    subsection "Not Enough Materials"

        text
            If a recipe cannot be crafted because you do not have enough materials, collect the missing resources before attempting the recipe again.
        end

    end

end

section "Important Notes"

    note
        Crafting recipes can change between Minecraft versions. This guide is intended for Minecraft Bedrock Edition.
    end

    note
        Some recipes are affected by the current game version, enabled features, or game settings.
    end

    note
        The recipe book is useful for discovering recipes, but learning common crafting patterns can make crafting faster.
    end

    note
        Not every item in Minecraft is created through the standard crafting grid.
    end

end

